WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.442
Survey data often arrives in long form with one row per respondent-question.

00:00:05.442 --> 00:00:09.307
If there is at most one score for each respondent and question,

00:00:09.307 --> 00:00:15.012
MAX can be used as a convenient aggregate to place that value into the correct column.

00:00:15.012 --> 00:00:19.067
The output grain becomes one respondent.

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:23.082
The Q1, Q2, and Q3 categories become columns.

00:00:23.082 --> 00:00:30.457
A pivot converts category values into columns, usually through conditional aggregation in portable SQL.

00:00:30.457 --> 00:00:34.057
Each target column needs a clear aggregation rule.

00:00:34.057 --> 00:00:40.212
Before pivoting, check whether the source contains more than one value for the same row-key and category

00:00:40.212 --> 00:00:41.038
combination.
